	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Date mediane]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=19969#p19969"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>PS : Finalement, la requête utilisée :</p><p>1/ Je crée la fonction médiane d&#039;après <a href="http://wiki.postgresql.org/wiki/Aggregate_Median" rel="nofollow">http://wiki.postgresql.org/wiki/Aggregate_Median</a>:</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>CREATE FUNCTION _final_median(anyarray) RETURNS float8 AS $$ 
  WITH q AS
  (
     SELECT val
     FROM unnest($1) val
     WHERE VAL IS NOT NULL
     ORDER BY 1
  ),
  cnt AS
  (
    SELECT COUNT(*) AS c FROM q
  )
  SELECT AVG(val)::float8
  FROM 
  (
    SELECT val FROM q
    LIMIT  2 - MOD((SELECT c FROM cnt), 2)
    OFFSET GREATEST(CEIL((SELECT c FROM cnt) / 2.0) - 1,0)  
  ) q2;
$$ LANGUAGE sql IMMUTABLE;
 
CREATE AGGREGATE median(anyelement) (
  SFUNC=array_append,
  STYPE=anyarray,
  FINALFUNC=_final_median,
  INITCOND=&#039;{}&#039;
);</code></pre></div><p>2/ Je l&#039;utilise dans mon cas bien particulier en définissant une date d&#039;origine antérieure à toute mes dates (en prenant le 1 mars 1900 dans mon cas) :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>SELECT num_year, id_station, txt_variety, txt_stage,
	cast(median(dat_stage-&#039;1900-03-01&#039;) as integer) + &#039;1900-03-01&#039;::date dat_stage_median
FROM t_plot JOIN t_stage ON t_plot.id_plot=t_stage.id_plot
GROUP BY num_year, id_station, txt_variety, txt_stage
ORDER BY num_year, id_station, txt_variety, txt_stage</code></pre></div><p>Encore merci.</p>]]></content>
